. It saves about 370 in daily order fees but pays about 760 more in storage. Around day 16 it also likely goes over the 252-unit warehouse limit and loses part of a delivery.\n- **Candidate 3** orders every second day at about the same factors as candidate 2. It saves about 286 in fees, pays about 340 more in storage, and gets a small benefit from pooling two days of stock. That is roughly a tie with candidate 2, possibly about 50 worse.\n\n**Candidate 0 compared with candidate 2.** The two plans are the same except at the start and the end.\n- **Start:** candidate 0 orders 20 extra units of product 0 on day 0, arriving on day 4. The starting stock (54 units of product 0) runs out on day 1, so stock is empty when the extra arrives. About 70% of those units get sold, a gain of about +70.\n- **End:** for the last deliveries it orders exactly the forecast: 11 fewer units of product 0 and 7 fewer of product 1 than candidate 2. By then a large surplus has built up, so those units would mostly have gone unsold. Cutting them gains about +130–150.\n\nThat puts candidate 0 about 200 ahead of candidate 2, and it is the most robust of the plans when demand moves away from the forecast."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:21:02.995Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBBwQioySPpCLVBQ8bxW"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QL7